      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Proponents of school vouchers argue they empower parents by providing financial aid to access private or religious schools, potentially improving educational options. They suggest this competition encourages public schools to improve their quality. Critics, however, oppose vouchers, arguing they drain essential funding from the public school system and often benefit wealthier families more. Many also worry that private schools receiving vouchers may not adhere to the same educational standards as public schools.",
